WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:09.320
AI agents are software systems that use an AI model to interpret a goal, reason through possible steps, use tools, access information, and perform actions.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:17.460
An agent may combine a model with orchestration code, application state, memory, APIs, files, and feedback from earlier steps.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:25.360
The model supplies language-based reasoning, but the surrounding software determines what the agent can reach and what consequences its output can create.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.780
A basic chatbot normally responds to one message with text that a person reviews.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.920
An agent may work through a multi-step loop: understand a request, select a tool, read a result, revise a plan, and take another action.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:46.500
It might search a knowledge base, draft a ticket, call a business API, update a workflow, or ask another service for information.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.200
That ability to act is the important difference from a simple conversational interface.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.660
Agent security matters because model behavior is connected to real capabilities.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:03.880
A mistaken interpretation, unsafe instruction, overly broad permission, or untrusted document can influence more than an answer on a screen.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:11.140
It may affect sensitive data, external communications, system configuration, business records, or other users.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:17.040
The impact depends on what tools, data, identities, and workflows the application exposes.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.700
A secure design treats the agent as a complete software system rather than as a self-contained model.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:31.480
Teams should map the model, orchestration layer, tools, data sources, memory, credentials, users, approvals, logs, and downstream systems.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:39.140
Once those components and trust boundaries are visible, developers and security teams can place controls where decisions become access or action.
